Z||000000||gt boy||09-25-2001||07:54 AM||||what type of special tools do i need to take all the body panels off of a fiero?<P>does any one have any pics of them disassembling a fiero?<P>how much work is it to do?<P>the reason i ask is that i have an car with a very nice red paint job ...and my other car that i want to keep has faded black paint that is peeling...i just thought that it would be a little cheaper to swap all the panels...does anyone see any problems with this?<P>------------------<BR>"it's too bad he had to run out of talent half way through the corner..."||||reg||5
Z||000001||mbramble||09-25-2001||08:59 AM||||No special tools are required.  10mm and 7mm socket and combo wrenches, and a set of torx wrenches.  <P>If you are going to swap out the roof panel and rear clip you will have to remove the headliner and the upper trim that helps to hold it in place.  <P>You may also want to check out rodneydickman.com, fierostore.com and <A HREF="http://www.ardeldistributors.com/catalog.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ardeldistributors.com/catalog.html</A>  for fasteners that you may need in case you break some during removal.  With careful removal you should be able to reuse most of them but the plastic rivets at the bottom of the door panel will have to be replaced.  You can use the 'christmas tree' type fasteners found in the 'Help!' section of most auto parts places to replace them with.||||reg||1
